.TH NOSTR-HOMED-PROVISION-VERIFY 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-homed-provision-verify \- fetch the current pointer and HEAD-check every chunk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-homed-provision verify
\fB\-\-account\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-relay\-timeout\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches the current kind-30078 pointer, decrypts the manifest, then issues a
Blossom HEAD to every server in the account list for every chunk hash. Reports
per-chunk replication counts.
.PP
Unlike
.BR nostr-homed-provision-pull (1),
verify never downloads a chunk body \(em it only probes for presence. This
makes it cheap enough to run from cron.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-account\-file \fIPATH\fR
0600 account file. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one JSON object per chunk on stdout (JSONL): chunk hash, size, per-server
status (HEAD result code plus latency). Otherwise a compact text table.
.TP
.B \-\-relay\-timeout\-ms \fIMS\fR
Total budget for the pointer fetch. Default 10000.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
All chunks are present on at least one server.
.TP 4
.B 2
Bad argument.
.TP 4
.B 5
At least one chunk is missing from every server. Details in the output.
.TP 4
.B 71
Network failure during pointer fetch.
.TP 4
.B 72
Manifest decode failure.
.TP 4
.B 75
Crypto failure (manifest decrypt).
.TP 4
.B 76
Internal error.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Nightly cron check with a machine-parseable JSON output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision verify \\
    \-\-account\-file ~/.config/nostr-homed/abcd1234.account.json \\
    \-\-json > /var/log/porthome-verify.$(date +%F).jsonl
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision-push (1)
